  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I will keep my mouth with a bridle, while the wicked is before me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "I was dumb with silence, I held my peace, even from good; and my sorrow was stirred.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "My heart was hot within me, while I was musing the fire burned: then spake I with my tongue,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "LORD, make me to know mine end, and the measure of my days, what it is: that I may know how frail I am.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Behold, thou hast made my days as an handbreadth; and mine age is as nothing before thee: verily every man at his best state is altogether vanity. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Surely every man walketh in a vain shew: surely they are disquieted in vain: he heapeth up riches, and knoweth not who shall gather them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "And now, Lord, what wait I for? my hope is in thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Deliver me from all my transgressions: make me not the reproach of the foolish.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "I was dumb, I opened not my mouth; because thou didst it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Remove thy stroke away from me: I am consumed by the blow of thine hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "When thou with rebukes dost correct man for iniquity, thou makest his beauty to consume away like a moth: surely every man is vanity. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear unto my cry; hold not thy peace at my tears: for I am a stranger with thee, and a sojourner, as all my fathers were.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:39:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "O spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go hence, and be no more.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 39:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:39:13"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
